            },
            "kind": "NO_CHANGE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This is going to conflict very heavily with https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/84608\n\nCan you please review the above, and we can look to build one set of code that works for both behaviors?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Somewhat meta question, Why are all these conditions important for the BMC to support?  Don't each of these mean that a certificate authority is authorizing certs that are invalid?\n\nNot against unit tests by any means, just trying to understand."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Igor Kanyuka",
                        "email": "ifelmail@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ifel"
                    },
                    "message": "Rebasing."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Igor Kanyuka",
                        "email": "ifelmail@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ifel"
                    },
                    "message": "Not quite. For example many of these tests test getUPNFromCert, which does not rely only on certificate authority, but also has logic extracting a username, so these tests aimed to test this logic and not certificate authority. I created them before touching the code in the following changes to make sure those change will not introduce regressions."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> getUPNFromCert, which does not rely only on certificate authority,\n\nThis is the part I don't understand.  The \"Cert\" in \"getUPNFromCert\" is coming from a certificate authority and was signed."
